@* The disclosure marker: a chevron that turns over when what it points at is open — the filter
   bar's panel, the setup form's fine-tune card, the statistics scope menu and its folded aspect
   rows, the seat picker, the spirit card's variants.

   Six of them spelled the rotation out as the same interpolated ternary, and the pair of
   utilities that make it turn *smoothly* had been written apart from it — so the marker was one
   forgotten `transition-transform` away from snapping round instead. Size and tone stay with the
   caller, since these run from a 12px mark inside a chip to the 16px one on a card's header. *@

<Icon Name="chevron-down" Class="@($"shrink-0 transition-transform {Class}{(Open ? " rotate-180" : "")}")"/>

@code {
    /// <summary>Whether what this points at is showing — turns the mark over.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Open { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Size and tone. The default is the one a card header or a field button wears.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string Class { get; set; } = "w-4 h-4 text-ink-400";
}
